October 21, 1999
MINUTES
WINNETKA VILLAGE COUNCIL
SPECIAL MEETING
(Approved November 2, 1999)
A record of a legally convened meeting of the Council of the Village of
Winnetka, which was held in the Village Hall Council Chamber on Thursday,
October 21, 1999, at 7:30 p.m.
I. Call to Order.
President Pro Tem Michael Duhl called the meeting to order at 7:35 p.m.
Present: Trustees Don Derning and John Lien. Absent: President Louise Holland
and Trustees Barbara Aquilino, David Hilton, and John Powell. Also present:
Village Manager Doug Williams, Director of Community Development Cindy
McCammack, and about seven persons in the audience.
II. Pledge of Allegiance.
President Pro Tem Duhl led the group in pledging allegiance to the flag.
III. Approval of the Agenda.
The Council approved the Agenda as drafted.
IV. Public Hearing – Draft Comprehensive Plan
President Pro Tem Duhl declared the Public Hearing open, noting that this was
the third Public Hearing on the proposed Comprehensive Plan, and asked Ms.
McCammack to read the public notice, which she did. Ms. McCammack reported that
staff is in the process of updating street maps of the Village clearly
identifying collector and primary streets and that updated traffic information
is also expected prior to introduction of the Plan on November 2, 1999.
There was a question from the floor regarding the lack of inclusion of cost
estimates in the Plan. Ms. McCammack explained that the purpose of the Plan is
to provide guidance for the Council and staff over an extended time period and
that, therefore, any estimated costs would quickly become obsolete and be
irrelevant over the life of the document. Manager Williams commented that it is
the responsibility of the Village Manager and staff to incorporate the
objectives and goals of the Plan into the Budget as feasible given the
availability of funds. Mr. Duhl noted that there are always more possible
projects than there is money to finance them, and that the Village Council with
the counsel of the Manager and staff have to establish the priorities.
There being no further questions from the floor, President Pro Tem Duhl closed
the Public Hearing.
V. Adjournment.
Trustee Lien moved to adjourn the meeting, and Trustee Derning seconded the
motion. By voice vote, the motion carried unanimously. The meeting adjourned at
7:43 p.m.
