MINUTES
WINNETKA VILLAGE COUNCIL MEETING
A record of a legally convened meeting of the Council of the Village of
Winnetka, which was held in the Village Hall Council Chamber on Tuesday,
December 7, 1999, at 7:30 p.m.
I. Call to Order.
President Louise Holland called the meeting to order at 7:33 p.m. Present:
Trustees Barbara Aquilino, Don Derning, David Hilton, John Lien, and John
Powell. Absent: Trustee Michael Duhl. Also present: Acting Village Manager Ed
McKee, Village Attorney Katherine Janega, Director of Community Development
Cindy McCammack, and about three persons in the audience.
II. Pledge of Allegiance.
President Holland led the group in pledging allegiance to the flag.
III. Approval of the Agenda.
The Council approved the Agenda as drafted.
IV. Quorum.
December 14, 1999, Study Session. All of the Trustees present, except Trustee
Hilton, indicated that they would be able to attend.
December 21, 1999, Regular Meeting. All of the Trustees present indicated that
they would be able to attend.
V. Approval of Minutes
November 16, 1999, Regular Meeting. Trustee Derning, seconded by Trustee
Hilton, moved to adopt the minutes as drafted. By voice vote, the motion
carried unanimously.
VI. Public Comment and Questions.
None
VII. Ordinances and Resolutions
Ordinance No. M-593-99 – Zoning Variation: 552-554 Lincoln Ave. - Adoption.
Trustee Lien, seconded by Trustee Hilton, moved to adopt the ordinance
permitting an amendment to an existing Special Use Permit to allow the
expansion of first floor office space resulting from the realignment of the
front building line. By roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes:
Trustees Derning, Aquilino, Powell, Hilton, and Lien. Nays: None. Absent:
Trustee Duhl.
Ordinance No. M-594-99 – Zoning Variation: 132 Fuller Ln. - Adoption. Trustee
Powell, seconded by Trustee Hilton, moved to adopt the ordinance permitting an
increase in the intensity of use of lot and maximum building size. By roll call
vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Derning, Aquilino, Powell,
Hilton, and Lien. Nays: None. Absent: Trustee Duhl.
Ordinance No. M-596-99 – Special Use Permit: Winnetka Park District, Temporary
Offices - Adoption. Trustee Hilton, seconded by Trustee Lien, moved to adopt
the ordinance permitting the temporary location of modular office units
alongside A.C. Neilsen Tennis Center. By roll call vote, the motion carried
unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Derning, Aquilino, Powell, Hilton, and Lien. Nays:
None. Absent: Trustee Duhl.
Ordinance No. M-597-99 – Zoning Variation: 5 Indian Hill Rd. - Introduction.
Ms. McCammack reviewed the request to permit structural alterations to allow
new window openings in an existing non-conforming corner setback which will
facilitate a change in the interior layout of the residence. She noted that the
Zoning Board of Appeals had voted 5-0 to recommend approval of the requested
variation.
The applicant, Dan Gill responded to questions from the Trustees.
Trustee Powell expressed his thanks to the Gills for taking on a project of
this magnitude to restore the home for all of the Village.
Trustee Derning, seconded by Trustee Powell, moved to introduce the ordinance.
By voice vote, the motion carried.
Ordinance No. M-598-99 – Zoning Variation: 757 Locust St. - Introduction. Ms.
McCammack reviewed the request to permit replacement of an existing roof and
construction of new dormers located within front and corner setbacks. She noted
that the Zoning Board of Appeals had voted 5-0 to recommend approval of the
requested variation.
Trustee Derning confirmed that the existing building lines are not affected,
and Trustee Powell inquired as to whether the steeper pitch of the roof would
affect the home’s height. Ms. McCammack responded that it would, but that it
would still be less than the maximum 35 ft. limit. Ms. Janega noted that the
ordinance includes a finding as to the new building height and added that the
specific locations of the roof and dormers are addressed in the conditions for
the variation.
Trustee Aquilino, seconded by Trustee Powell, moved to introduce the ordinance.
By voice vote, the motion carried.
VIII. Unfinished Business.
None
IX. New Business
Warrant Lists Nos. 1151 and 1152. Trustee Powell moved to approve Warrant List
No. 1151 in the total amount of $450,165.36 and Warrant List No. 1152 in the
total amount of $424,347.35. Trustee Derning seconded the motion. By roll call
vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Powell, Hilton, Lien,
Derning, and Aquilino. Nays: None. Absent: Trustee Duhl.
Preauthorization of Purchase of Three Squad Cars. Chief William Gallagher
explained that the Police Department had recently received the State of
Illinois bid for police squad vehicles. He said that the department expects to
purchase three new squad cards from the 2000-2001 Fiscal Year Budget as
replacements for current vehicles and that in order to insure both the price
and delivery times indicated on the bid, orders must be placed during December,
1999. He noted that the state bid price for the cars, equipped with the options
traditionally ordered, will be approximately $21,000 per car.
Trustee Derning, seconded by Trustee Powell, moved to authorize the purchase of
the three squad cars. By roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes:
Trustees Derning, Aquilino, Powell, Hilton, and Lien. Nays: None. Absent:
Trustee Duhl.
Payment of Special Assessment for Cherry Street Alley. At 7:52 p.m. Trustee
Derning moved to recess from the Regular Council meeting to convene as the
Board of Local Improvements for the purpose of considering the Certificate of
Costs submitted by DiPaolo and considering the adoption of Resolution SA-1-99
authorizing payments for the improvements to the public alley between Ash and
Cherry Streets, from Locust to Rosewood. The motion was seconded by Trustee
Aquilino. By roll call vote, the motion passed unanimously. Ayes: Trustees
Derning, Lien, Aquilino, Hilton, and Powell. Nays: None. Absent: Trustee Duhl.
The Trustees reconvened into Regular Session at 8:04 p.m. Present: Trustees
Aquilino, Derning, Hilton, Lien, and Powell. Absent. Trustee Duhl. Also
present: Acting Village Manager Ed McKee and Village Attorney Katherine Janega.
Trustee Derning, seconded by Trustee Lien, moved to authorize the purchase of
the Special Assessment No. 296 vouchers from DiPaolo Company, in a total amount
of not more than $35,307.00. By roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously.
Ayes: Trustees Derning, Aquilino, Powell, Hilton, and Lien. Nays: None. Absent:
Trustee Duhl.
X. Reports
Village President. President Holland reported that she and Nan Greenough had
met with Art Schmidt from The Bellows regarding the restoration of the
chandeliers and sconces in the Council Chambers and that the project would
begin soon.
Village Trustees. Trustee Lien noted the distribution of the final, fully bound
copies of Winnetka 2020. Trustee Derning reported on his attendance at a RED
Center meeting. He indicated that the organization is continuing to explore
relocation possibilities.
XI. Appointments.
President Holland expressed thanks to Jack Wentz and Ann Alexander for their
service on the Plan Commission and suggested the appointment of Bob Horne and
Becky Hurley, respectively, as their replacements.
Trustee Hilton, seconded by Trustee Lien, moved to approve the appointments. By
voice vote the motion carried unanimously.
XII. Executive Session.
Trustee Hilton moved to adjourn into Executive Session for the purpose of
discussing pending and probable litigation, personnel matters, and the possible
sale of Village owned land, pursuant to Section 2(c)(11), 2(c)(1), and 2(c)(6),
respectively, of the Illinois Open Meetings Act. Trustee Aquilino seconded the
motion. By roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously: Ayes: Trustees
Aquilino, Derning, Duhl, Hilton, Lien, and Powell. Nays: None. Absent: None.
The Council convened into Executive Session at 8:15 p.m.
The Council reconvened into Regular Session at 8:47 p.m. Present: President
Holland, Trustees Aquilino, Derning, Duhl, Hilton, Lien, and Powell. Absent:
None. Also present: Village Manager Williams and Village Attorney Janega.
XIII. Adjournment.
Trustee Hilton moved to adjourn the meeting and Trustee Powell seconded the
motion. By voice vote, the motion carried unanimously. The meeting adjourned at
8:50 p.m.
