President Duhl noted that the Landmark Preservation Commission had proposed
Jane Burns as its representative to the Beautification Committee and called for
a motion to approve that recommendation. Trustee Presser so moved, seconded by
Trustee Aquilino. By voice vote, the motion carried unanimously
12. Executive Session.
Trustee Presser moved to adjourn into Executive Session for the purpose of
discussing pending and probable litigation, personnel matters, the possible
purchase of property, and the possible sale of Village owned land, pursuant to
Section 2(c)(11), Section 2(c)(1), Section 2(c)(5), and 2(c)(6), respectively,
of the Illinois Open Meetings Act. Trustee Powell seconded the motion. By roll
call vote, the motion carried unanimously: Ayes: Trustees Aquilino, Brower,
Greenough, Powell, Presser, and Woodbury. Nays: None. Absent: None. The Council
convened into Executive Session at 10:30 p.m.
The Council reconvened into Regular Session at 10:50 p.m. Present: President
Duhl, Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Greenough, Powell, Presser, and Woodbury.
Absent: None. Also present, Village Manager Doug Williams.
13. Adjournment.
Trustee Brower, seconded by Trustee Presser, moved to adjourn the meeting. By
roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Aquilino,
Powell, Presser, Greenough, Woodbury, and Brower. Nayes: None. Absent: None.
The meeting adjourned at 10:51 p.m.
