awarded to Anthony Scopelliti Landscaping at $34,849.31 per year.
Trustee Brower, seconded by Trustee Presser, moved to award the bids, as
recommended. By roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees
Brower, Presser, Aquilino, Powell, Woodbury, and Greenough. Nays: None. Absent:
None.
d)   Outdoor Seating Permits and Sidewalk Restaurant Liquor License Riders.
Manager Williams explained that this is the annual renewal of the outdoor
seating permit applications for the following eight restaurants: Caribou
Coffee, Starbucks, J.P. McCarthy’s, The Sweet Shop, Song O’Sixpence, Caffe Buon
Giorno, Corner Cooks, and St. Louis Bread/Panera.
Additionally, he noted that applications for renewal of the sidewalk restaurant
liquor license riders for J.P. McCarthy’s and Corner Cooks were up for
consideration. He reported that there had been no significant complaints last
year about outdoor liquor service and indicated that staff recommended
approval.
Trustee Presser, seconded by Trustee Woodbury, moved to approve the outdoor
seating permits and sidewalk restaurant liquor license riders as applied for.
By roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Presser,
Aquilino, Powell, Woodbury, Greenough, and Brower.
10. Reports.
Manager: Mr. Williams reported that the Village would be opening bids for the
Village Yards Project on April 30th. He said that he hoped to have
recommendations to the Council by early May for the groundworking contract.
He also reported that the Village had once again received a Certificate of
Achievement for Excellence in Accounting from the Government Finance Office and
thanked the Finance Director and his staff for their efforts to achieve this
recognition.
Trustees. Trustee Brower reported that he attended a luncheon at the Winnetka
Community House during which there was a presentation on the proposed new
building and an update on fundraising efforts. He commented that theirs is an
ambitious program and that the plans are attractive. He indicated that he and
Trustee Aquilino also had attended a Chamber of Commerce meeting.
Trustee Powell reported on his attendance at a recent NWMC meeting during which
various topics of interest were covered.
President: President Duhl reported that he met with members of the Interfaith
Housing Council regarding affordable housing options. He suggested that
interested persons might tune into a series of dialogues on the topic to be
presented throughout the region on WTTW. He said that interested individuals
could participate locally on April 22nd from 7:30 p.m. to 8:00 p.m. at St.
Francis Xavier Church, 808 Linden, Wilmette.
President Duhl congratulated Trustee Brower on his selection as Man of the Year
by the Chamber of Commerce, saying it was a richly deserved honor.
11. Appointments.
President Duhl suggested the reappointment of Mark Crane to the Zoning Board of
Appeals for a second full term. Trustee Woodbury, seconded by Trustee Powell,
moved to approve the appointment. By voice vote, the motion carried
unanimously.
President Duhl then suggested the appointment of Christopher Rintz to the
Building Review Committee for a three-year term. Trustee Presser, seconded by
Trustee Aquilino, moved to approve the appointment. By voice vote, the motion
carried unanimously.
Finally, President Duhl suggested the appointment of Barbara Aquilino to the
Canvassing Board for the March 19th election. Trustee Brower, seconded by
Trustee Greenough, moved to approve the appointment. By voice vote, the motion
carried unanimously.
12. Executive Session.
Trustee Aquilino moved to adjourn into Executive Session for the purpose of
discussing pending and probable litigation, and personnel matters, pursuant to
Section 2(c)(11), and Section 2(c)(1), respectively, of the Illinois Open
Meetings Act. Trustee Powell seconded the motion. By roll call vote, the motion
carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Brower, Greenough, Aquilino, Presser, and
Woodbury. Nays: None. Absent: None. The Council convened into Executive Session
at 8:30 p.m.
The Council reconvened into Regular Session at 9:11 p.m. Present: President
Duhl, Trustees Brower, Greenough, Aquilino, Powell, Presser, and Woodbury.
Absent: None. Also present, Village Manager Douglas Williams and Village
Attorney Katherine Janega.
13. Adjournment.
Trustee Brower, seconded by Trustee Greenough, moved to adjourn the meeting. By
roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Aquilino,
Powell, Presser, Greenough, Woodbury, and Brower. Nays: None. Absent: None. The
meeting adjourned at 9:12 p.m.
