President Duhl suggested the appointment of Brad McLane to serve out the term
of Mary Lambert who recently resigned from the Plan Commission. Trustee
Presser, seconded by Trustee Aquilino, so moved. By voice vote, the motion
carried unanimously
President Duhl suggested the appointment of Maureen Mitchell as the School
Board’s representative to the Plan Commission to replace Becky Hurley. Trustee
Aquilino, seconded by Trustee Woodbury, so moved. By voice vote, the motion
carried unanimously
7. Executive Session.
Trustee Woodbury moved to adjourn into Executive Session for the purpose of
discussing pending and probable litigation, personnel matters, and board
appointments, pursuant to Sections 2(c)(11), and Section 2(c)(1), and Section 2
(c)(3), respectively, of the Illinois Open Meetings Act. Trustee Presser
seconded the motion. By roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes:
Trustees Aquilino Brower, Greenough, Woodbury, Powell, and Presser. Nays: None.
Absent: None. The Council convened into Executive Session at 9:15 p.m.
8. The Council reconvened into Regular Session at 10:55 p.m.
Present: President Duhl and Trustees Aquilino, Brower, Greenough, Powell,
Presser and Woodbury. Absent: None. Also present, Village Manager Douglas
Williams and Village Attorney Katherine Janega.
9. Adjournment.
Trustee Aquilino, seconded by Trustee Greenough, moved to adjourn the meeting.
By roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Aquilino,
Woodbury, Greenough, Powell, Presser, and Brower. Nays: None. Absent: None. The
meeting adjourned at 10:56 p.m.
