January 10, 2004
MINUTES
WINNETKA VILLAGE COUNCIL SPECIAL MEETING
(Approved: January 20, 2004)
A record of a legally convened meeting of the Council of the Village of
Winnetka, which was held at 419 Sheridan Road, Winnetka, Illinois, on Saturday,
January 10, 2004 at 3:00 p.m.
1. Call to Order.
The meeting began at 3:05 p.m. when Trustees David Abell, Hugh Brower, Stephen
Presser, and Nan Greenough met at 419 Sheridan Road.
2. Tour of Home Proposed for Landmark Preservation: 419 Sheridan Road.
The owner, Mr. Muneer Satter conducted a tour of his property that is being
considered for Landmark status. He showed the Trustees the restored exterior,
including the wrought iron railings and the metal and glass entry as well as
the new family room addition. He pointed out that in order to achieve a
seamless transition from the old house to the new addition, salvaged limestone
had been used on the east façade. Mr. Satter explained that the gardens and
walls have been restored as well, with new terraces incorporating limestone
balustrades and blue stone pavements to match those already existing. He
mentioned that while restoring the main, original terrace on the east of the
house, a structurally unsound, secret room underneath the terrace had been
discovered.
Mr. Satter also showed the Trustees the interior restoration work in the first
floor public spaces and the reconfigured living space over the garage.
3. Adjournment.
The meeting adjourned at 3:55 p.m.
