Business Community Development Commission Tom Eilers
Chamber of Commerce                       Tom Eilers
Museum Liaison                            Herb Ritchell
NW Municipal Conference                   Nan Greenough
Plan Commission                           Jessica Tucker
Red Center                                Dave Abell
                                          Dave Webster (alt)
SWANCC                                    Mike Duhl
                                          Doug Williams
Warrants Review                           Dave Abell
Winnetka Report                           Jessica Tucker
Youth                                     Herb Ritchell
 
13. Quorum
a)   April 13, 2004, Study Session. All of the Trustees present indicated that
they expected to attend.
b)   April 20, 2004, Regular Meeting. All of the Trustees present indicated
that they expected to attend.
14. Executive Session.
Trustee Ritchell moved to adjourn into Executive Session for the purpose of
discussing pending and probable litigation, personnel matters, and board
appointments, pursuant to Sections 2(c)(11), and Section 2(c)(1), and Section 2
(c)(3), respectively, of the Illinois Open Meetings Act. Trustee Abell seconded
the motion. By roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees
Abell, Eilers, Greenough, Ritchell, Webster, and Tucker. Nays: None. Absent:
None. The Council convened into Executive Session at 8:55 p.m.
The Council reconvened into Regular Session at 9:38 p.m. Present: President
Duhl, Trustees Abell, Tucker, Greenough, Ritchell, Webster, and Eilers. Absent:
None. Also present, Village Manager Douglas Williams and Village Attorney
Katherine Janega.
15. Adjournment.
Trustee Tucker seconded by Trustee Webster, moved to adjourn the meeting. By
roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Abell, Brower,
Greenough, Woodbury, Webster, and Presser. Nays: None. Absent: None. The
meeting adjourned at 9:39 p.m.
