February 1, 2005
MINUTES
WINNETKA VILLAGE COUNCIL
REGULAR MEETING
(Approved: February 15, 2005)
A record of a legally convened meeting of the Council of the Village of
Winnetka, which was held in the Village Hall Council Chamber on Tuesday,
February 1, 2005 at 7:30 p.m.
1. Call to Order.
President Pro Tem Nan Greenough called the meeting to order at 7:32 p.m.
Present: Trustees David Abell, Tom Eilers, Herb Ritchell, and Jessica Tucker.
Absent: President Michael Duhl. Also present: Village Manager Doug Williams,
Village Attorney Katherine Janega, Finance Director Ed McKee, Director of
Public Works Steve Saunders and six persons in the audience, including Trustee
Candidates Ken Behles and Sandra Berger.
2. Pledge of Allegiance.
President Pro Tem Greenough led the group in the Pledge of Allegiance.
3. Approval of the Agenda.
The Council approved the Agenda, as drafted.
4. Quorum.
a)   February 8, 2005, Study Session. All of the Council members present,
except for Trustee Abell, indicated that they expected to attend.
b)   February 15, 2005, Regular Meeting. All of the Council members present
indicated that they expected to attend.
5. Village Council Minutes.
a)   January 11, 2005, Study Session. Trustee Ritchell moved to adopt the
minutes, as drafted. Trustee Abell seconded the motion. By voice vote, the
motion carried unanimously.
b)   January 18, 2005, Regular Meeting. Trustee Abell asked that the name of
the committee mentioned in Item 12(a) be corrected. Trustee Eilers moved to
adopt the minutes, as corrected. Trustee Tucker seconded the motion. By voice
vote, the motion carried unanimously.
6. Ordinances and Resolutions.
a)   Ordinance No. M-01-2005 – Zoning Variation: 766 Prospect - Adoption.
President Pro Tem Greenough called for a motion to adopt this ordinance
granting a variation from the intensity of use of lot and maximum building size
requirements of the zoning ordinance to permit the construction of a mudroom
addition and front porch to the home at 766 Prospect Ave. Trustee Woodbury so
moved, seconded by Trustee Tucker. By roll call vote, the motion carried
unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Woodbury, Ritchell, Abell, Eilers, Tucker, and
Greenough. Nays: None. Absent: President Duhl.
b)   Ordinance No. M-02-2005 – Zoning Variation: 458 Sunset – Adoption.
President Pro Tem Greenough call for a motion granting variations from the
intensity of use of lot, building line articulation and side yard setback
provisions of the Zoning Ordinance to permit the construction of a second floor
addition at the rear of the home at 458 Sunset. Trustee Woodbury so moved,
seconded by Trustee Ritchell. By roll call vote, the motion carried
unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Woodbury, Ritchell, Abell, Eilers, Tucker, and
Greenough. Nays: None. Absent: President Duhl.
c)   Resolution No. R-04-2005 – Bluhm Subdivision: Final Plat Approval –
Adoption. Trustee Abell moved to remove the matter from the table. Trustee
Ritchell seconded the motion. By voice vote, the motion carried unanimously.
Ms. Janega reviewed the modified language included in the draft resolution.
Trustee Tucker raised a question about the wording of the restrictive covenant
regarding secondary access, saying that she believed that some provisions had
been omitted.
Mr. Shenk, Mr. Bluhm’s attorney, stated that he believed that the proposed
language was correct.
Ms. Janega indicated that she would need to go back to check her notes to
verify its accuracy.
Trustee Abell, therefore, moved that the matter be tabled until the February
15th meeting. Trustee Tucker seconded the motion. By voice vote, the motion
carried unanimously.
d)   Resolution No. R-03-2005 – Easement Agreement with SBC for Community Event
Sign Kiosk – Adoption. Ms. Janega explained that the resolution authorizes the
fifteen-year agreement negotiated between the Village and SBC for use of the
southwest corner of Linden and Green Bay for a community information kiosk. She
reviewed the Village’s options should SBC find it necessary to have the
facility moved or altered. Ms. Janega also mentioned that the Village had
reached agreement with the Chamber as to their use of one panel.
Trustee Eilers thanked SBC for their willingness to permit the Village to
continue to use their property and moved to approve the resolution. Trustee
Ritchell seconded the motion. By roll call vote, the motion carried
unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Eilers, Tucker, Woodbury, Ritchell, Abell, and
Greenough.
7. Old Business.
None.
8. New Business.
a)   Warrant Lists Nos. 1399 and 1400. Trustee Tucker reviewed the Warrant
Lists. After commenting on a number of the items, Trustee Ritchell moved to
approve Warrant List No. 1399 in the amount of $1,018,673.40 and Warrant List
No. 1400 in the amount of $279,109.75. Trustee Eilers seconded the motion. By
roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Abell, Eilers,
Greenough, Ritchell, Tucker and Woodbury. Nays: None. Absent: President Duhl.
9. Public Comment and Questions.
None.
10. Reports.
None.
11. Appointments.
None.
12. Executive Session.
Trustee Eilers moved to adjourn into Executive Session for the purpose of
discussing pending and probable litigation, personnel matters, and board
appointments pursuant to Section 2(c)(11), Section 2(c)(1), and 2(c)(3)
respectively, of the Illinois Open Meetings Act. Trustee Tucker seconded the
motion. By roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees
Abell, Eilers, Greenough, Ritchell, Tucker and Woodbury Nays: None. Absent:
President Duhl. The Council convened into Executive Session at 7:55 p.m.
The Council reconvened into Regular Session at 8:41 p.m. Present: President Pro
Tem Greenough, Trustees Abell, Eilers, Ritchell, Tucker and Woodbury. Absent:
President Duhl. Also present, Village Manager Doug Williams and Village
Attorney Katherine Janega.
13. Adjournment.
Trustee Ritchell, seconded by Trustee Woodbury, moved to adjourn the meeting.
By roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Abell,
Eilers, Greenough, Ritchell, Tucker and Woodbury. Nays: None. Absent: President
Duhl. The meeting adjourned at 8:42 p.m.
