MINUTES
WINNETKA VILLAGE COUNCIL
SPECIAL MEETING
(Approved: April 18, 2006)
A record of a legally convened meeting of the Council of the Village of
Winnetka, which was held in the Village Hall Council Chambers on Tuesday, April
11, 2006, at 7:30 p.m.
1. Call to Order.
President Woodbury called the meeting to order at 7:38 p.m. Present: Trustees
David Abell, Ken Behles and Jessica Tucker. Absent: Trustees Berger, Eilers and
Ritchell. Also present: Village Manager Doug Williams, Village Attorney
Katherine Janega, Finance Director Ed McKee, Acting Director of Water &
Electric Rich Ciesla, Fire Chief Scott Smith, Chief of Police Joe DeLopez and
approximately 4 persons in the audience.
2. Pledge of Allegiance.
President Woodbury led the group in the Pledge of Allegiance.
3. Approval of the Agenda.
The Trustees approved the Agenda as drafted.
4. Ordinances and Resolutions.
a)   Ordinance No. MC-2-2006 – Amending Hours for Class C Liquor Licenses -
Adoption. Village Attorney Janega reviewed the amendments to Chapter 5.09 of
the Village Code, which would allow alcoholic beverages to be sold until 2:00
a.m. at special events held in certain types of facilities, but would preserve
the 10:00 p.m. limitation for outdoor events. As a result of the discussion at
time of introduction, technical amendments were made as well to standardize the
references to Class C licenses throughout the ordinance. Ms. Janega also
clarified the Village President’s authority to limit the hours of sale in
response to a question from Trustee Behles.
