                                   Doug Williams
Train Station Liaison              Ken Behles
Warrants Review                    Herb Ritchell
                                   Sandy Berger
Winnetka Report                    Ken Behles
 
a)   Trustees.
Trustee Eilers announced that the Business Community Development Commission
would be meeting on Thursday morning, with the agenda including discussions of
parking needs and solutions and a property maintenance code. He encouraged
interested persons to attend the meeting scheduled for 7:30 a.m. in the Council
Chambers.
Trustee Behles reported that Metra had presented a preliminary design schedule
for work on the Elm Street train station. He indicated that he and staff intend
to meet with Metra in hopes of keeping the project moving forward.
Trustee Berger reported that RED Center Board of Directors has approved the
development of a web site and marketing materials for the purpose of soliciting
membership.
Trustee Abell reported on a recent NWMC meeting. He said that it appears that
the DROP legislation will not resurface until next year’s legislative session.
He advised that the NWMC is studying a new bill (COPE) in Congress that would
establish national franchising for cable and telephone vendors which could
impact the Village’s ability to control its rights-of-way, and that the Village
President had sent letters to our legislators in Washington opposing the COPE
proposal.
12. Executive Session.
Trustee Ritchell moved to adjourn into Executive Session for the purpose of
discussing pending and probable litigation, personnel matters, board
appointments, and review of Executive Session Minutes pursuant to Sections 2(c)
(11), 2(c)(1), and 2(c)(3), respectively, of the Illinois Open Meetings Act.
Trustee Tucker seconded the motion. By roll call vote, the motion carried
unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Abell, Behles, Berger, Eilers, Tucker, and
Ritchell. Nays: None. Absent: None. The Council convened into Executive Session
at 8:45 p.m.
The Council reconvened into Regular Session at 10:15 p.m. Present: President
Woodbury, Trustees Abell, Behles, Eilers, Tucker, Ritchell, and Berger. Absent:
None. Also present: Village Manager Doug Williams and Village Attorney
Katherine Janega.
13. Adjournment.
