Recording Secretary
July 18, 2006
MINUTES
WINNETKA VILLAGE COUNCIL
REGULAR MEETING
(Approved: August 1, 2006)
A record of a legally convened meeting of the Council of the Village of
Winnetka, which was held in the Village Hall Council Chambers on Tuesday, July
18, 2006, at 7:30 p.m.
1. Call to Order.
President Woodbury called the meeting to order at 7:37 p.m. Present: Trustees
David Abell, Ken Behles, and Herb Ritchell, Absent: Trustees Sandra Berger, Tom
Eilers, and Jessica Tucker. Also present: Village Manager Doug Williams,
Village Attorney Katherine Janega, Assistant Director of Community Development,
Brian Norkus, Director of Public Works Steve Saunders, and approximately three
persons in the audience.
2. Pledge of Allegiance.
President Woodbury led the group in the Pledge of Allegiance.
3. Approval of the Agenda.
The Trustees approved the Agenda as drafted.
4. Quorum.
a)   August 1, 2006, Regular Meeting. All of the Council members present,
except Trustees Abell and Ritchell, indicated that they expected to attend.
b)   August 8, 2006, Study Session. All of the Council members present, except
Trustee Abell and President Woodbury, indicated that they expected to attend.
5. Village Council Minutes.
a)   July 6, 2006, Regular Meeting. Trustee Abell moved to approve the minutes
as drafted. Trustee Ritchell seconded the motion. By voice vote, the motion
carried unanimously.
6. Ordinances and Resolutions.
a)   Ordinance No. M-13-2006 – Zoning Variations: 445 Sheridan Rd. - Adoption.
After Attorney Janega responded to a question from Trustee Abell about the
property’s legal description, President Woodbury called for a motion to adopt
this ordinance granting three zoning variations to permit the expansion and
remodeling of an existing coach house at 445 Sheridan Road. Trustee Ritchell so
moved, seconded by Trustee Behles. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes:
Trustees Ritchell, Abell, and Behles and President Woodbury. Nays: None.
Absent: Trustees Eilers, Tucker and Berger.
b)   Ordinance No. M-14-2006 – Zoning Variations: 902 Spruce Street - Adoption.
There being no further comments, President Woodbury called for a motion to
adopt this ordinance granting two zoning variations to permit the
reconstruction of the front entry and deck at 902 Spruce Street. Trustee Behles
so moved, seconded by Trustee Abell. By roll call vote, the motion carried.
Ayes: Trustees Behles, Ritchell, and Abell and President Woodbury. Nays: None.
Absent: Trustees Eilers, Tucker and Berger.
c)   Ordinance No. M-15-2006 – Special Use Permit & Zoning Variations: 874
Green Bay Rd. - Adoption. Attorney Janega reviewed proposed amendments to the
draft ordinance correcting references to the existing antennas on the property.
Trustee Ritchell, seconded by Trustee Abell, moved to amend the ordinance as
discussed by the Village Attorney. By voice vote, the motion carried
unanimously.
President Woodbury called for a motion to adopt this ordinance, as amended,
granting a Special Use Permit and two zoning variations to permit the
installation of a wireless telecommunication service facility on the building
at 874 Green Bay Road. Trustee Ritchell so moved, seconded by Trustee Abell. By
roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Ritchell, Abell, and Behles
and President Woodbury. Nays: None. Absent: Trustees Eilers, Tucker and Berger.
d)   Ordinance No. MC-4-2006 – Amending the Flood Hazard Area Regulations
Pertaining to the Use of Retaining Walls – Adoption. Trustee Behles asked
whether given the complexity of the ordinance and the number of acronyms it
would be helpful to add a definition section. Attorney Janega replied that
there is a significant definition section in the Village Code that is not
normally repeated in individual sections in order to avoid the necessity of
updating in multiple places.
There being no further comments, President Woodbury called for a motion to
adopt this ordinance amending the Flood Hazard Area regulations pertaining to
retaining walls by limiting (1) the ground elevation where basements may be
constructed, (2) the height of retaining walls, and (3) the slopes used to
achieve grade changes made necessary by the elevation of the building pad.
Trustee Abell moved to adopt Ordinance MC-40-2006, seconded by Trustee Behles.
By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Abell, Behles and
Ritchell and President Woodbury. Nays: None. Absent: Trustees Eilers, Tucker,
and Berger.
e)   Resolution No. R-18-2006 – Approval of Development Agreement: 934 Westmoor
Road – Adoption. Mr. Norkus reviewed the proposal to construct a 2-1/2 story,
three-unit town home development to replace the existing single family
residence located in the B-1 multiple family district at 934 Westmoor Road. He
noted that the proposed development complies with all zoning regulations and
received a Certificate of Appropriateness from the Design Review Board. He
explained that the Village Code requires that developers of such projects
execute a development agreement with the Village detailing measures of
protection to be taken by the developer to control the impact of construction
on neighbors and the Village. Resolution R-18-2006 would approve the
Development Agreement between the Village and Westmoor Commons, LLC, pertaining
to the development of the subject property.
Trustee Ritchell confirmed with Mr. Norkus that no variations are required in
order to proceed with the development. He said that he believes that this is a
good use of space in the zoning corridor.
Trustee Ritchell then asked how the Agreement was developed. Attorney Janega
replied that the Agreement began with the provisions of agreements previously
approved and then modified according to the specifics of this development.
Finally, Trustee Ritchell expressed concern about mud being left in the street
and, given the corner location, the ability of pedestrians to pass the
construction site safely. He suggested that very specific language be added to
the ordinance. Ms. Janega pointed out that the mobilization plan lays out
pedestrian access and spells out duration and time of sidewalk closures, and
Trustee Behles commented that the property line is well off the property so
that fencing shouldn’t be a problem.
Trustee Abell, seconded by Trustee Behles, moved to adopt Resolution No. R-18-
2006 approving the Development Agreement between the Village and Westmoor
Commons, LLC, in a form substantially comparable to proposed draft. By roll
call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Abell, Behles, and Ritchell and
President Woodbury. Nays: None. Absent: Trustees Eilers, Tucker and Berger.
7. Public Comment and Questions.
None.
8. Old Business.
None.
9. New Business.
a)   Warrant Lists Nos. 1469 and 1470. Trustee Ritchell reviewed the Warrant
Lists. After commenting on a number of the items, he moved to approve Warrant
List No. 1469 in the amount of $734,857.94 and Warrant List No. 1470 in the
amount of $710,676.39. Trustee Behles seconded the motion. By roll call vote,
the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Abell, Behles and Ritchell, and President
Woodbury. Nays: None. Absent: Trustees Eilers, Tucker and Berger.
b)   Bid No. 06-021: Refuse Truck Purchase (PW-34). Mr. Saunders reviewed the
bids for the purchase of a new refuse truck to replace an existing truck in
poor condition. He recommended the purchase of a new Freightliner chassis and a
new Pak-More body from R.N.O.W., Inc., whose bid meets all of the village’s
specifications, in the amount of $97,009.50.
Trustee Ritchell, seconded by Trustee Behles, moved to approve the bid as
recommended. By voice vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees
Ritchell, Abell and Behles, and President Woodbury. Nays: None. Absent:
Trustees Eilers, Tucker, and Berger.
10. Reports.
a)   Trustees. Trustee Behles reported on a recent follow-up meeting with Metra
regarding the Elm Street train station renovation. He said that although no
representative from Union Pacific was present, the Village received some
reassurance that the project would proceed in the direction previously
approved, including the installation of new elevators. However, some unresolved
issues remain, such as shelter and light design and bridge repair. He noted
that Metra’s desire not to expand their land use onto any more of Union
Pacific’s land will impact some of the design elements already approved: Mr.
Behles pointed out that no funding commitment has yet been made.
b)   President. President Woodbury reported on a meeting he attended regarding
the status of the Willow Road project through Northfield and Glenview. He noted
that a number of high-ranking officials were in attendance and numerous items
were discussed, including capacity, aesthetics, and safety (vehicular and
pedestrian). He indicated that he expects there will be some sort of an
agreement as to direction by the end of this year, but construction is still a
couple of years out because of the design process and funding issues. He
complimented Senator Schoenberg on his efforts to find a consensus among the
parties.
c)   Manager. Manager Williams reported that the electric system had hit a new
production peak during the week. He also reported that the Tax Assessor’s
office had advised the Village of the final numbers for the property tax levy
and noted that if the Village were not home rule, the property tax levy for
2005 could be 5.1%, which is higher than the 4.5% set by the Council, so the
Village is under what tax caps would have allowed.
Manager Williams then asked Mr. Saunders and Mr. Stier to update the Council on
the discovery of Emerald Ash Borers in the vicinity, which they did.
11. Appointments.
None.
12. Executive Session.
Trustee Behles moved to adjourn into Executive Session for the purpose of
discussing pending and probable litigation and Board appointments pursuant to
Sections 2(c)(11) and 2(c)(3), respectively, of the Illinois Open Meetings Act.
Trustee Abell seconded the motion. By roll call vote, the motion carried
unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Behles, Ritchell and Abell, and President Woodbury.
Nays: None. Absent: Trustees Eilers, Tucker, and Berger. The Council convened
into Executive Session at 8:50 p.m.
The Council reconvened into Regular Session at 9:30 p.m. Present: President
Woodbury, Trustees Abell, Behles, and Ritchell. Absent: Trustees Eilers,
Tucker, and Berger. Also present: Village Manager Doug Williams and Village
Attorney Katherine Janega.
13. Adjournment.
Trustee Ritchell, seconded by Trustee Behles, moved to adjourn the meeting. By
roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Abell, Behles
and Ritchell, and President Woodbury. Nays: None. Absent: Trustees Eilers,
Tucker, and Berger. The meeting adjourned at 9:31 p.m.
