single-phase and Wesco for the three-phase transformers.
Trustee Poor, seconded by Trustee Tucker, moved to award the purchase orders
for the acquisition of single-phase transformers from Resco and three-phase
transformers from Wesco, for a total amount not to exceed $95,215.00. By roll
call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Behles, Berger, Eilers, Poor,
Ritchell and Tucker. Nays: None. Absent: None.
f)   Letter of Understanding: Willow Road Study: President Woodbury reported
that discussions between the Villages of Winnetka and Northfield have
culminated in an agreement for a joint planning exercise for various
infrastructure improvements to Willow Road. He said the Villages will co-
sponsor a study, which will develop a public process for the formulation of a
Willow Road plan to benefit both Villages and the regional corridor. He
indicated that a request for funding had been sent to Senator Schoenberg, and
the Village expects to be reimbursed for its part of the study’s cost.
Trustee Behles, seconded by Trustee Tucker, moved to authorize the Village
President to sign the Willow Road letter of understanding with the Village of
Northfield. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Behles,
Berger, Eilers, Poor, Ritchell and Tucker. Nays: None. Absent: None.
g)   Rescheduling of July 3rd Council Meeting: Manager Williams reported that
the first regularly scheduled Council meeting in July falls on July 3. He
observed that since many people celebrate the July Fourth holiday on that day,
the Council may wish to consider rescheduling its meeting. After discussing
their options, the Council decided to reschedule the meeting and hold it
immediately before the July 10th Study Session.
Trustee Poor, seconded by Trustee Berger, moved to reschedule the July 3
meeting for July 10. By voice vote, the motion carried.
12)   Reports.
a)   Trustees. Trustee Berger reported that at the last NWMC meeting, there was
