MINUTES
WINNETKA VILLAGE COUNCIL REGULAR MEETING
(Approved: May 20, 2008)
A record of a legally convened meeting of the Council of the Village of
Winnetka, which was held in the Village Hall Council Chambers on Tuesday, May
6, at 7:30 p.m.
1)   Call to Order.
President Woodbury called the meeting to order at 7:39 p.m. Present: Trustees
Ken Behles, Sandra Berger, Tom Eilers, King Poor, Herb Ritchell and Jessica
Tucker. Absent: None. Also present: Village Manager Doug Williams, Village
Attorney Katherine Janega, Director of Public Works Steve Saunders, Director of
Water & Electric Brian Keys, Trustees-elect Gene Greable, Bill Johnson and
Chris Rintz, and approximately 15 persons in the audience.
2)   Pledge of Allegiance.
President Woodbury welcomed Winnetka Boy Scout Troop 20 to the meeting, and led
the group in the Pledge of Allegiance.
3)   Approval of the Agenda.
President Woodbury suggested moving the public comment until after the new
Council is seated. The Trustees approved the agenda as amended.
4)   Quorum.
a)   May 13, 2008, Study Session. All of the non-retiring Council members
present, as well as the three Trustees-elect, indicated that they expected to
attend.
b)   May 20, 2008, Regular Meeting. All of the non-retiring Council members
present, as well as the three Trustees-elect, indicated that they expected to
attend.
5)   Village Council Minutes.
a)   April 15, 2008,Regular Meeting. Trustee Behles suggested some
clarifications to the minutes relating to the zoning variance request for 455
Sheridan. Trustee Ritchell, seconded by Trustee Tucker, moved to approve the
minutes with the amendments suggested by Trustee Behles. By voice vote, the
amended minutes were approved.
6)   Ordinances and Resolutions.
a)   Ordinance No. M-6-2008 – Zoning Variation: ––––616 Garland Avenue–––
Adoption. President Woodbury reviewed the subject ordinance, introduced at the
April 15 th meeting, which would grant three zoning variations to permit a one-
story addition and front-facing garage doors, and called for additional
comments.
There being none, Trustee Poor, seconded by Trustee Behles, moved to adopt
Ordinance No. M-6-2008. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees
Behles, Berger, Eilers, Poor, Ritchell and Tucker. Nays: None. Absent: None.
b)   Ordinance No. MC-2-2008 – Village Code Amendments Regarding Revisions to
Flood Hazard Protection Ordinance – Adoption. President Woodbury explained that
the subject ordinance would amend the Village Code to reflect revisions made by
FEMA to maps and elevations. He indicated that the changes will not affect the
“footprint” of Winnetka’s floodplain, and called for additional questions or
comments.
There being none, Trustee Ritchell, seconded by Trustee Behles, moved to adopt
Ordinance MC-2-2008. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees
Behles, Berger, Eilers, Poor, Ritchell and Tucker. Nays: None. Absent: None.
* * * *
