b)   Ratification of Salt Purchase Decision. Manager Williams explained that
the Village relies on a joint purchasing program through the State to procure
its annual supply of de-icing salt. However, this year road salt is in short
supply in the Midwest, and salt suppliers have been unable or unwilling to
commit to providing the State with adequate supplies. As a result the cost of
salt has changed repeatedly and risen substantially, to more than double the
amount budgeted for the current fiscal year. He asked Mr. Saunders to update
the Trustees on the current status of the Village’s salt supply, order for the
coming winter, options, and ongoing efforts to minimize the use of salt, which
