MINUTES
WINNETKA VILLAGE COUNCIL
REGULAR MEETING
January 6, 2009
(Approved: Approved January 20, 2009)
A record of a legally convened meeting of the Council of the Village of
Winnetka, which was held in the Village Hall Council Chambers on Tuesday,
January 6, 2009, at 7:30 p.m.
1)   Call to Order.
President called the meeting to order at 7:35 p.m. Present: Trustees Ken
Behles, Sandra Berger, Gene Greable, Bill Johnson, King Poor and Chris Rintz.
Absent: None. Also present: Village Manager Doug Williams, Village Attorney
Katherine Janega, Public Works Director Steve Saunders. There was no one in the
audience.
2)   Pledge of Allegiance.
President Woodbury led the group in the Pledge of Allegiance.
3)   Approval of the Agenda.
The Trustees approved the agenda as presented.
4)   Quorum.
a)   January 13, 2009 Study Session. All of the Council members present
indicated that they expected to attend.
b)   January 19, 2009, Special Meeting. All of the Council members present
indicated that they expected to attend.
   January 20, 2009, Regular Meeting. All of the Council members present
indicated that they expected to attend.
5)   Village Council Minutes.
a)   December 2, 2008 Regular Meeting. President Woodbury and Trustee Behles
suggested minor changes to the draft minutes that were agreed to by the
Council. Thereafter Trustee Berger, seconded by Trustee Poor, moved to approve
the minutes. By voice vote, the motion carried.
6)   Ordinances and Resolutions.
None.
7)   Public Comment and Questions.
None.
8)   Old Business.
None.
9)   New Business.
a)   Warrant Lists 1587 and 1588. Trustee Johnson reviewed the Warrant Lists.
After commenting on a number of the items, he moved to approve Warrant List No.
1587 in the amount of $914,630.71 and Warrant List No. 1588 in the amount of
$595,247.58. The motion was seconded by Trustee Behles. By roll call vote, the
motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Behles, Berger, Greable, Johnson, Poor and
Rintz. Nays: None. Absent: None.
b)   Village Hall Rehabilitation – Architect Selection. Mr. Saunders reviewed
the progress of the Village Hall Rehabilitation project, which is estimated to
cost $2.9 million if all the recommended interior and exterior elements are
implemented. He then explained the bid selection process used to choose an
architectural consultant to perform the necessary architecture design services,
and recommended awarding the contract to Holarbird & Root, LLC.
Responding to a question from Trustee Poor, Mr. Saunders stated that the
Village would be looking for some level of LEEDs certification for the work.
After further discussion, Trustee Behles, seconded by Trustee Johnson, moved to
award a contract to Holarbird & Root, LLC, to perform professional
architectural services for modernization and restoration of the Winnetka
Village Hall, for a lump sum fee not to exceed $257,000. By roll call vote, the
motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Behles, Berger, Greable, Johnson, Poor and
Rintz. Nays: None. Absent: None.
10)   Reports
a)   Village President. None
b)   Trustees. None
c)   Attorney. None
d)   Manager. None
11)   Appointments.
None.
12)   Executive Session.
Trustee Berger moved to adjourn into Executive Session for the purpose of
discussing Pending and Probable Litigation, Board Appointments and Personnel
Matters, pursuant to Sections 2(c)(11), 2(c)(3), and 2(c)(1) of the Open
Meetings Act.   Trustee Poor seconded the motion. By roll call vote, the motion
carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Behles, Berger, Greable, Johnson, Poor and
Rintz. Nays: None. Absent: None. The Council adjourned into Executive Session
at 7:48 p.m.
The Council reconvened into Regular Session at 9:25 p.m. Present: President
Woodbury, Trustees Behles, Berger, Greable, Johnson, Poor and Rintz. Absent:
None. Also present: Village Manager Doug Williams and Village Attorney
Katherine Janega.
13)   Adjournment.
Trustee Rintz, seconded by Trustee Behles, moved to adjourn the meeting. By
roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Behles, Berger, Greable,
Johnson, Poor, and Rintz. Nays: None. Absent: None. The meeting adjourned at 9:
26 p.m.
