set forth by the Plan Commission.
   Carolyn Kurtz, Park Board President, Bob Smith, Parks Superintendent, and
Colin Marshall, the architect, presented the plan to the Trustees. Ms. Kurtz
related that the Park District has worked diligently for four years and studied
numerous options in an effort to better serve Winnetka and protect its assets
and open space, and that this plan reflects the combined efforts of the Village
and the Park Board to come together for the common good.
   After the Park Board’s representatives responded to questions from the
Trustees, Trustee Poor, seconded by Trustee Rintz, moved to amend the ordinance
as discussed by the Village Attorney. By voice vote, the motion carried.
   Trustee Greable, seconded by Trustee Johnson, then moved to waive
