      v)   Trustee Poor reported that the Environmental and Forestry Commission
has started to work on a list of priorities.
   b)   Village President. President Tucker commented on the success of the
Fourth of July celebration. She also announced that there will be a ceremony in
the fall to rededicate the newly refurbished Cenotaph. Finally, she raised the
question of writing to the Village’s representatives regarding the potential
closing of the Hubbard Woods Post Office as requested by a Hubbard Woods
property owner. There were no objections to doing so.
   c)   Attorney. None.
   d)   Manager. None.
11)   Appointments.
   a)   President Tucker called for a motion to appoint Ken Behles, Mark
