also noted that she had attended a preliminary meeting with Village staff at
New Trier High School to discuss their expansion plans as well as a request
from New Trier to partner with the Village on a parking facility in Indian
Hill. She indicated that, given the expense of such a plan, and the parking
deficit in the East Elm business district, it would be difficult to find
consensus for spending a large sum of money for an Indian Hill parking project.
   b)   Trustees.
      i)   Trustee Greable reported that he had attended a Chamber of Commerce
meeting last week, where it was disclosed that CVS is inquiring about renting
space in the West Elm business district.
      ii)   Trustee Spinney reported that she had attended the Library Board
meeting, where they discussed investments, and plan on taking a poll of other
government bodies in the Village to see what their investment strategies are.
      iii)   Trustee Johnson announced that the BCDC would meet this Thursday
at 7:30 AM.
   c)   Attorney. Attorney Janega reported that the plaintiff’s motion to
reconsider the dismissal of LaBella v. Winnetka had been denied. She also
reported that the City of Chicago had filed a response to the NRA’s petition to
the U.S. Supreme Court on the handgun case, and that Winnetka may file an
