call vote. the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Poor, Johnson, Rintz, Pedian, and
Greable. Nays: None. Absent: Trustee Spinney.
4)   Ordinances and Resolutions.
   a)   Resolution No. R-34-2009 – Authorizing the Issuance of a Class E-
2 Liquor License to The ––––Winnetka–– Wine Shop, LLC – Adoption. Attorney
Janega reported that this is the second applicant to request a liquor license
under the recently established Class E-2. She explained that the request is for
a specialty wine shop to be called The Winnetka Wine Shop, and noted that the
application follows the standards for the E-2 license classification since the
classification was established at the request of this applicant and it was
built around her description of her business model. She added that the
background check has been completed, and that successful completion of the
remaining premises inspections is required as a condition for authorization and
issuance of the license.
There was a brief discussion about the application. The applicant, Emily Link,
answered a few questions from the Trustees and clarified that the three two-
ounce servings would not be available for tastings, but would accompany food
service. Attorney Janega stated that the clarification will be noted on the
license.
Trustee Pedian, seconded by Trustee Rintz, moved to adopt Resolution R-34-2009,
