Greable, seconded by Trustee Johnson, moved to approve the amendments as
reviewed by the Village Attorney. By voice vote, the motion carried. Trustee
Spinney, seconded by Trustee Johnson, moved to adopt Ordinance MC-7-2009 as
amended. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Greable,
Johnson, Pedian, Poor, and Spinney. Nays: None. Absent: Trustee Rintz.
   b)   Resolution No. R-4-2010 – ––––Willow–– Road Federal Aid Rehabilitation
Amendment to Phase I Engineering. As noted earlier, this item was removed from
the Agenda.
7)   Public Comment and Questions.
None. (No members of the public were in attendance.)
8)   Old Business.
None.
9)   New Business.
   a)   Water Plant Dehumidification Unit Bids. Mr. Keys noted that high
humidity in the basement area of the Water Plant, known as the “pipe gallery,”
is causing deterioration of the fittings and equipment in the vicinity. He
reviewed the bid responses for the purchase of a desiccant dehumidifier unit
for the pipe gallery, noting that the low bidder quoted alternate equipment
that deviated from the bid specifications, resulting in their bid being
disqualified. He recommended issuance of a purchase order to the lowest
qualified bidder, G.V. Zintel Associates, Inc. He responded to questions from
the Trustees and mentioned that separate contracts will be issued at a later
date for the ductwork and pad construction necessary for installation of the
dehumidifier.
Trustee Greable, seconded by Trustee Johnson, moved to award a purchase order
to G.V. Zintel Associates, Inc., in the amount of $43,975 for the purchase of a
Munters dehumidification unit. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes:
Trustees Greable, Johnson, Pedian, Poor, and Spinney. Nays: None. Absent:
Trustee Rintz.
