President Tucker then proposed reappointing Peggy Swartchild to a second full
term on the Business Community Development commission. Trustee Johnson,
seconded by Trustee Spinney, moved to so appoint Ms. Swartchild. By voice vote,
the motion carried.
12)   Executive Session.
Trustee Poor moved to adjourn into Executive Session to discuss Personnel and
Pending and Probable Litigation, pursuant to Sections 2(c)(1) and 2(c)(11)
respectively, of the Illinois Open Meetings Act. Trustee Johnson seconded the
motion. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Greable, Johnson,
Pedian, Poor, Rintz and Spinney. Nays: None. Absent: None. The Council
adjourned into Executive Session at 9:50 p.m.
The Council reconvened into Regular Session at 11:40 p.m. Present: President
Tucker, Trustees Greable, Johnson, Pedian, Poor, Rintz and Spinney. Absent:
None. Also present: Village Manager Doug Williams and Village Attorney
Katherine Janega.
13)   Adjournment.
Trustee Rintz, seconded by Trustee Spinney, moved to adjourn the meeting. By
roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Greable, Johnson, Pedian,
Poor, Rintz and Spinney. Nays: None. Absent: None. The meeting adjourned at 11:
41 p.m.
            
