   d)   Manager. None.
11)   Appointments.
   a)   President Tucker suggested the reappointment of Richard Glenn to the
Police Pension Board for a full term, upon the expiration of his current term.
Trustee Johnson, seconded by Trustee Spinney, moved to reappoint Mr. Glenn to
the PPB. By voice vote, the motion carried.
   b)   President Tucker suggested the reappointment of Lawson Whitesides to
the Environmental & Forestry Commission for a full term, upon the expiration of
his current term. Trustee Poor, seconded by Trustee Pedian, moved to reappoint
Mr. Whitesides to the EFC. By voice vote, the motion carried.
   c)   President Tucker next recommended the reappointment of Lawson
Whitesides as the Environmental & Forestry Commission’s representative to the
Plan Commission at the beginning of his second term. Trustee Pedian, seconded
by Trustee Poor, moved to so appoint Mr. Whitesides. By voice vote, the motion
