Rintz seconded the motion. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes:
Trustees Greable, Johnson, Pedian, Poor, Rintz and Spinney. Nays: None. Absent:
None. The Council adjourned into Executive Session at 8:30 p.m.
The Council reconvened into Regular Session at 8:48 p.m. Present: President
Tucker, Trustees Greable, Johnson, Pedian, Poor, Rintz and Spinney. Absent:
None. Also present: Interim Village Manager Liz Rosenthal and Village Attorney
Katherine Janega.
Attorney Janega submitted the order affirming the decision of Chief Smith and
said once the Council vote is taken, it would be entered on the order and the
order would be sent to the parties.
Trustee Poor, seconded by Trustee Johnson, moved to issue the Council’s written
opinion and final order in the form discussed by the Council. By roll call
vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Poor, Johnson, Spinney, Rintz, Pedian,
and Greable. Nays: None. Absent: None.
   b)   Ruling: Glenn Weaver Fire Code Appeal. Attorney Janega reported that
this appeal is another compliance issue with the fire sprinkler requirement,
