MINUTES
WINNETKA VILLAGE COUNCIL
SPECIAL MEETING
September 29, 2010
(Approved: October 5, 2010)
A record of a legally convened meeting of the Council of the Village of
Winnetka, which was held in the Village Hall Council Chambers on Wednesday,
September 29, 2010, at 7:30 p.m.
1)   Call to Order.
President Tucker called the meeting to order at 7:31 p.m. Present: Trustees
Gene Greable, Bill Johnson, Linda Pedian, King Poor, Chris Rintz and Jennifer
Spinney. Absent: None. Also present: Interim Village Manager Liz Rosenthal,
Village Attorney Katherine Janega, and approximately 30 persons in the
audience.
2)   Pledge of Allegiance.
President Tucker led the group in the Pledge of Allegiance.
3)   Ordinance MC-6-2010: Village Manager Residency – Introduction and
Adoption.
Village Attorney Katherine Janega noted that the ordinance number had been
corrected to MC-8-2010. She reviewed the amendment to Section 2.12.010 of the
Village Code that provides that the Council set by resolution the time period
within which the Village Manager must establish residency in the Village after
appointment. Because of the need to move promptly with the appointment of the
Village Manager, Ms. Janega said that the Council could waive introduction of
the ordinance which requires a unanimous vote and then move for adoption.
Trustee Johnson, seconded by Trustee Pedian, moved to waive introduction of
Ordinance MC-8-2010. By roll call vote, the motion passed unanimously. Ayes:
Trustees Poor, Johnson, Spinney, Rintz, Pedian, and Greable. Nays: None.
Absent: None.
Trustee Greable, seconded by Trustee Johnson, moved to adopt Ordinance MC-8-
2010 amending Section 2.12.010(C) of the Village Code to provide that the
Council set by resolution the time period for the Village Manager to establish
residency in the Village after appointment. By roll call vote, the motion
carried. Ayes: Trustees Poor, Johnson, Spinney, Rintz, Pedian, and Greable.
Nays: None. Absent: None.
4)   Appointment of Village Manager.
President Tucker nominated Robert M. Bahan for appointment to Village Manager.
Trustee Rintz, seconded by Trustee Pedian, moved to approve the appointment. By
roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Poor, Johnson, Spinney,
Rintz, Pedian, and Greable. Nays: None. Absent: None.
5)   Resolution R-34-2010 – Agreement Establishing the Terms and Conditions of
the Village Manager’s Employment.
Village Attorney Janega noted that this resolution would approve the terms of
the employment contract negotiated with Mr. Bahan.
There were no questions or comments.
Trustee Johnson, seconded by Trustee Pedian, moved to adopt Resolution R-34-
2010 establishing the terms and conditions of the Village Manager’s employment.
By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Poor, Johnson, Spinney,
Rintz, Pedian, and Greable. Nays: None. Absent: None.
President Tucker thanked the consultants, former village presidents, and
department heads for their assistance and support throughout the process to
select a Village Manager. She welcomed Mr. Bahan, noting that he becomes the 6
th Village Manager of Winnetka and is a veteran of public management who has
served in Clarendon Hills as Village Manager since 2002.
Each of the Trustees then made welcoming remarks to Mr. Bahan.
6)   Adjournment.
President Tucker invited all present to remain for a brief welcoming reception
for Mr. Bahan immediately following adjournment.
Trustee Johnson, seconded by Trustee Spinney, moved to adjourn the meeting. By
roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Greable, Johnson, Pedian,
Poor, Rintz and Spinney. Nays: None. Absent: None. The meeting adjourned at 7:
56 p.m.
         
