   a)   Village President. President Tucker reported that Monday’s
Intergovernmental Forum had been a very interesting discussion, and she thanked
Attorney Janega and Manager Rosenthal for their hard work behind the scenes to
make the meeting a success. She designated Trustee Rintz as the Council’s
liaison for the stormwater management strategy project, and also reported that
on Nov. 8 she would attend a to discuss the Metra train scheduling process that
will take place in advance of its bridge construction project. She reminded
residents to rake their leaves onto the parkways for collection, as piling them
in the street creates a hazard.
   b)   Trustees.
      i)   Trustee Poor encouraged residents to attend the Veteran’s Day event
at the Winnetka Womans Club on November 11 at 5PM.
      ii)   Trustee Rintz reported that the Plan Commission continues to work
on Affordable Housing and it is hoped to have a report finalized in December.
      iii)   Trustee Johnson welcomed residents to attend the next BCDC meeting
on Nov. 11.
   c)   Attorney. No report.
   d)   Manager. Manager Rosenthal asked Mr. Saunders to brief the Council on a
recent MWRD workshop he attended. Mr. Saunders reported that permits for Cook
County’s wastewater treatment plants are up for renewal in the near future, and
the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency is considering possible changes in its
permit requirements for these facilities. He said the issue of reducing inflow
and infiltration of the sanitary sewer system is being examined, and he
explained that the presence of inflow waters into the sanitary sewer systems
cause basement backups and sanitary sewer overflows. As a result, the MWRD is
considering passage of new rules stipulating that no leakage be allowed into
the sanitary sewer systems, which could potentially result in large expenses
for homeowners and the Village. He discussed the situation briefly with the
Council and said he would keep them updated on developments as they occur.
11)   Appointments.
   President Tucker suggested the appointment of Chuck Dowding as the EFC’s
liaison to the Plan Commission, effective immediately. Trustee Poor, seconded
by Trustee Rintz, moved to so appoint Mr. Dowding. By voice vote, the motion
carried.
