   President Tucker announced that the wire pulling bid was being removed from
the Consent Agenda and would be considered separately later in the Agenda.
   Trustee Johnson, seconded by Trustee Spinney, moved to approve the Agenda,
as modified. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Poor,
Johnson, Spinney, Rintz, and Greable. Nays: None. Absent: Trustee Pedian.
5)   Consent Agenda
   a)   Village Council Minutes. None.
   b)   Warrant Lists Nos. 1699 and 1670. Approving Warrant List No. 1699 in
the amount of $1,681,026.02 and Warrant List No. 1670 in the amount of
$686,325.23.
   c)   Bid #011-011: Directional Boring. Authorizing the Village Manager to
execute a purchase order for directional boring work to B-Max, Inc. in an
amount not to exceed $507,400.00, in accordance with the terms and conditions
of Bid #011-011 .
   d)   Bid #011-012: Wire Pulling. [Removed from Consent Agenda for separate
vote.]
   e)   2011 Concrete Repair Program: Municipal Partnering Bid. Awarding a
contract to Schroeder and Schroeder for the 2011 Concrete Repair Program, in
the amount of $110,006.00.
   Trustee Poor, seconded by Trustee Johnson, moved to approve the foregoing
items on the Consent Agenda by omnibus vote. By roll call vote, the motion
carried. Ayes: Trustees Poor, Johnson, Spinney, Rintz, and Greable. Nays: None.
Absent: Trustee Pedian.
6)   Ordinances and Resolutions
   a)   Ordinance MC-4-2011: Amending Class E-2 Liquor License – Hours and
Eligibility for Sidewalk Restaurant Rider License – Introduction/Adoption.
Attorney Janega reviewed the draft ordinance amending the Village’s Liquor
Ordinance pertaining to the Class E-2 liquor license to expand hours to allow
an E-2 licensee to open at 9:00 AM on Saturdays and to be eligible for a
sidewalk restaurant license. She noted that in order for this Council to adopt
this ordinance, it must waive introduction and proceed to adoption. She noted
that the Village has not yet received an application from The Wine Shop for the
sidewalk service.
   Trustee Johnson, seconded by Trustee Spinney, moved to waive introduction of
Ordinance MC-4-2011. By roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes:
Trustees Johnson, Spinney, Greable, Poor, and Rintz. Nays: None. Absent:
Trustee Pedian.
   Trustee Poor, seconded by Trustee Johnson, moved to adopt Ordinance MC-4-
2011 amending the Village Liquor Control regulations to make Class E-
2 licensees eligible to obtain a Sidewalk Restaurant Rider License, and to
allow a business with a Class E-2 license to open at 9:00 AM on Saturdays. By
roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Poor, Spinney,
Greable, Johnson, and Rintz. Nays: None. Absent: Trustee Pedian.
   b)   R-22-2011: Authorizing a Sidewalk Restaurant Rider License for the
Winnetka Wine Shop, LLC. Trustee Johnson, seconded by Trustee Spinney, moved to
adopt Resolution R-22-2011, authorizing a Sidewalk Restaurant Rider License for
the Winnetka Wine Shop. By roll call vote, the motion carried unanimously.
Ayes: Trustees Poor, Johnson, Spinney, Rintz, and Greable. Nays: None. Absent:
Trustee Pedian.
   Trustee Spinney, seconded by Trustee Johnson, moved to approve an Outdoor
Seating Permit for the Winnetka Wine Shop provided it obtains the required
approvals from the appropriate Village Departments. By voice vote, the motion
carried unanimously.
* * *
   c)   Bid #011-012: Wire Pulling. [See item 5)c), above. Removed from Consent
Agenda for separate consideration.] Mr. Keys reviewed the bids and noted that
the low bidder, Western Utility Contractors, had informed him this afternoon
that they would like to withdraw their bid. He explained that the bid documents
specifically state that a contractor cannot modify or withdraw its bid within
60 days after the bid opening, and recommended that the Council award the
contract as bid. He then responded to questions from the Trustees.
   Attorney Janega agreed that the bid could not be revoked and explained that
the allowing the successful bidder to walk away after seeing other bids were
higher, would undermine the public bid process. She added that once the Council
officially awards the contract, the successful contractor is obliged to
proceed.
   After a brief discussion, Trustee Poor, seconded by Trustee Johnson, moved
to authorize the Village manager to execute a purchase order for wire pulling
services to Western Utility Contractors in an amount not to exceed $140,393, in
accordance with the terms and conditions of Bid #011-012. By roll call vote,
the motion carried unanimously. Ayes: Trustees Poor, Greable, Johnson, Rintz
and Spinney. Nays: None. Absent: Trustee Pedian.
