      v)   Trustee Fessler said she was part of an evaluation team, along with
Trustee McCrary, Manager Bahan, Finance Director McKee and two representatives
of the Bogdahn Group, the Village's investment consultant, that met to
interview prospective bond managers. The results of the interviews will be
discussed at next week's Study Session.
   c)   Attorney. Attorney Janega announced that the lawsuit filed by Farmers
Insurance against 104 local government entities has been dropped by the
plaintiff.
   d)   Manager. After congratulating Tom Fritts, Manager Bahan said the
legislative session in Springfield has ended, and local governments were
successful in holding off some key legislation, including minimum staffing of
fire departments. Local revenues were also preserved, but not much was done
with respect to budget.
13)   Executive Session.
Trustee Krucks moved to adjourn into Executive Session to discuss Pending and
Probable Litigation, pursuant to Section 2(c)11, of the Illinois Open Meetings
