7)   Ordinances and Resolutions.
   a)   Ordinance No.MC-5-2015: Foreign Fire Insurance Board Receipt &
Disbursement of Funds-Introduction.
   Fire Chief Alan Berkowsky noted this Ordinance includes amendments to the
Village Code that reflect current practices of the Board, including the
handling of funds.
   After a brief discussion, Trustee Myers, seconded by Trustee McCrary moved
to introduce Ordinance No. MC-5-2015. By voice vote, the motion carried.
   b)   Ordinance No.MC-6-2015: Amending Winnetka Village Code Regarding Water
Conservation-Introduction.
   Water & Electric Director Brian Keys explained this Ordinance is required to
be in compliance with new Illinois Department of Natural Resources (IDNR)
regulations. Assistant Director of Community Development Brian Norkus addressed
how this new regulation would impact plumbing devices. Both Mr. Keys and Mr.
Norkus noted residents would be made aware of the new Code change and educated
on how best to comply. Mr. Keys continued that this new regulation does not
seek to be punitive and that in his tenure as Water & Electric Director any
household that was inadvertently not in compliance with water conservation
rules was made aware by Village staff and ultimately the issue was agreeably
resolved.
   The Council discussed how best to coordinate and require a non-consecutive
lawn watering policy. Trustee Fessler noted her concern that residents find an
amenable way to accommodate this new regulation with their lawn watering
system. Mr. Keys stated he would further consider the best way to implement
this new system and would return to Council for final consideration. Trustee
Myers, seconded by Trustee Prodromos, moved to introduce Ordinance No. MC-6-
2015. By voice vote, the motion carried.
