4)   Public Comment.
Pat Balsamo, 1037 Cherry. Ms. Balsamo asked what a special service area is and
why two were terminated. Manager Bahan explained that a special service area is
a local infrastructure improvement for a given area, which the residents who
benefit from the improvement agree to co-fund through a special tax levy for a
specified period of time. When the time period is up, it means the project is
paid for; therefore, the special tax levy is terminated.
