    Deputy Clerk
May 9, 2017
MINUTES
WINNETKA VILLAGE COUNCIL STUDY SESSION
(Approved: June 6, 2017)
A record of a legally convened meeting of the Council of the Village of
Winnetka, which was held in the Village Hall Council Chambers on Tuesday, May
9, 2017, at 7:00 p.m.
1)   Call to Order.
President Rintz called the meeting to order at 7:00 p.m. Present: Trustees
Andrew Cripe, Bob Dearborn, Penny Lanphier, Scott Myers, and Kristin Ziv.
Absent: None. Also in attendance: Village Manager Robert Bahan, Assistant
Village Manager Megan Pierce, Village Attorney Benjamin Schuster, Community
Development Director Mike D’Onofrio, Economic Development Coordinator Mike
Martella and 2 persons in the audience.
2)   Downtown Master Plan Discussion.
President Rintz announced that he would reconfigure the format of the Agenda
for Council meetings by moving Public Comment and Reports to the beginning of
the meeting, so audience members who want to make remarks do not have to sit
through the entire meeting to do so. He added that Study Sessions may at times
be scheduled immediately after very short Regular Meetings, for more effective
discussion of complicated issues.
President Rintz said the evening’s discussion would center around the roles of
the Downtown Master Plan (DMP) Task Force and the Council, and would also
determine the desired scope of professional consulting assistance and community
engagement. Referring to the Discussion Outline in the agenda materials, he
asked the Council for their thoughts about the composition of the Task Force.
Trustee Myers suggested adding DMP Steering Committee alumnus Bob Winter to the
Task Force, as he brings knowledge of development, perspective from other
communities, and an awareness of public-private partnerships. President Rintz
nominated former Plan Commission Chair Becky Hurley and Design Review Board
Chair John Swierk. The Council agreed that these nominees would be good
additions to the Task Force.
The Council agreed to appoint the following Task Force members: John Talty
(Chair), Meg Benson, Steve Hudson, Bob Winter, Becky Hurley, John Swierk, and
Trustee Myers as Council Liaison.
Trustee Lanphier suggested expanding some of study topics to include
subcommittees, both to provide more community engagement that results in public
ownership of the policy decisions, and to develop new civic talent.
Trustee Myers agreed some of the issues could use an expansion of the core Task
Force, but cautioned that it be done in a way that does not bog down the
process.
Trustee Ziv agreed that a subcommittee approach could drag the process out, and
she remarked that Teska did a stellar job with community involvement and
engagement as well as marketing.
President Rintz noted that while some of the conversations would need
tailoring, the Council has a good sense of the issues that will be
controversial and can create a process for those issues which recognizes the
importance of timeliness.
The Council next discussed Section 2 of the Discussion Outline dealing with
assignment of study topics:
(a) Streetscape Review and Update
It was agreed that the Task Force should undertake a validation of the existing
Streetscape Plan. Also assigned to the Task Force: a process to engage the
community on (b) Wayfinding & Signage; (c) Bike Racks; and (d) Parklet Design
and Locations. It was recommended that the Task Force work with Teska to move
the review forward, resolve contentious issues, and present the Council with a
set of thoroughly vetted recommendations.
(e) Zoning Entitlements
Community Development Director Mike D’Onofrio explained that Zoning
Entitlements are implementation matters such as special use permits, variations
and planned developments. He noted that Staff has a good understanding of what
has and has not worked in the past, and that with assistance from the Village
Attorney, the standards for entitlements could be reduced and clarified. The
Council agreed with his recommendation; they also assigned item (g) Refine the
Design Review Process to Village Staff, the Design Review Board and the Village
Attorney, and assigned item (h) Implement Administrative Approval for Minor
Commercial Variations, to Staff and the Village Attorney.
(f) Commercial Overlay Districts
The Council had a lengthy discussion of the options, including a discussion of
land uses and objectives. It was agreed that the Task Force will get assistance
from Teska to facilitate a discussion about uses and objectives in the context
of Winnetka’s retail overlay district, and report their findings and
recommendations to the Council.
(j) Establish a Planned Development Commission
Attorney Schuster explained that the process for creating such a commission is
fairly standard, and the Council agreed to assume responsibility for this item
and for (j) Establishing a Fee-in-Lieu for Parking Relief, with the help of the
Village Attorney.
(k) Board/Commission Training
Manager Bahan said Staff would create a program, with assistance from the
Village Attorney and the American Planning Association.
(m) Public Improvement Standards for New Development
President Rintz, with the concurrence of the Council, assigned these
discussions to the Council. He explained that setting standards would reduce
time spent on negotiations when a Planned Development application is received,
and they could be made a part of the Planned Development Ordinance. Item (n)
Maintenance Options for Commercial Districts was also assigned to the Council.
Finally, the Council briefly discussed Item 3: Future Topics. It was agreed
that the jurisdictional transfer of Green Bay and Sheridan Roads would be an
assignment for the Task Force, resulting in recommendations for the Council. It
was decided that a Study Session discussion about whether to keep the Post
Office site or sell it needs to take place before any other considerations
about the site can be discussed.
3)   Public Comment.
None.
4)   Closed Session.
None.
5)   Adjournment.
Trustee Myers, seconded by Trustee Cripe, moved to adjourn the meeting. By
voice vote, the motion carried. The meeting adjourned at 9:25 p.m.
____________________________
