Quorum.
September 4, 2018 Regular Meeting. All of the Council members present said they
expect to attend.
September 13, 2018 Rescheduled Study Session. All of the Council members
present except Trustees Wedner and Dearborn said they expect to attend.
September 18, 2018 Regular Meeting. All of the Council members present except
Trustee Swierk said they expect to attend.
Public Comment.
Maddie O’Brien, 510 Meadow Road. Ms. O’Brien explained that she lived near New
Trier High School and Joseph Sears in Kenilworth, and that motorists use her
street as a shortcut when school lets out. She asked the Village to consider
putting a stop sign at an intersection near her home, in the interest of
pedestrian safety.
President Rintz asked Chief Hornstein to assign an officer to investigate the
area and advise the Public Works Department about whether a stop sign is
needed.
Rick Swanson, an architect from Lake Forest, said he is interested in
developing a property at 688-694 Green Bay Road, and he would like to gauge the
Council’s opinion on the feasibility of the plan. He presented a rendering of
the proposed six-unit building, and briefly described the development. The
Trustees gave their suggestions, and were generally in favor of Mr. Swanson
applying for the required permits and going through the Village’s approval
process.
Reports:
Trustees.
