During the Council discussion, the possibility of having code infractions dealt
with in Administrative Adjudication rather than going to the courts was brought
up. Manager Bahan said the hearing process could be modified at any time; and
President Rintz commented that the Village’s Administrative Law Judge might not
have broad enough powers to deal with extreme cases of noncompliance.
After their discussion, the Council was in favor of adopting the Subject
Ordinance.
There being no public comment, Trustee Cripe, seconded by Trustee Swierk, moved
to adopt Ordinance No. MC-5-2019. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes:
Trustees Coladarci, Cripe, Dearborn, Lanphier, Swierk, and Wedner. Nays: None.
Absent: None.
Old Business.
None.
New Business.
None.
Appointments:
None.
Closed Session.
Trustee Cripe moved to adjourn into Closed Session to discuss Collective
Bargaining, Sale or Lease of Village Property, and Pending or Probable
Litigation, pursuant to Sections 2c(2), 2c(5) and 2c(11), respectively, of the
Illinois Open Meetings Act. Trustee Wedner seconded the motion. By roll call
vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Coladarci, Cripe, Dearborn, Lanphier,
Swierk, and Wedner. Nays: None. Absent: None.
President Rintz announced that the Council would not return to the open meeting
after Executive Session. The Council adjourned into Executive Session at 8:55
p.m.
Adjournment.
Trustee Wedner, seconded by Trustee Cripe, moved to adjourn the meeting. By
