items on the Consent Agenda by omnibus vote. By roll call vote, the motion
carried. Ayes: Trustees Cripe, Apatoff, Dearborn, Dalman and Mancini. Nays:
None. Absent: Trustee Swierk.
8)   Ordinances and Resolutions.
   a)   Ordinance No. MC-5-2021: Amending Liquor Code (Introduction).
   Marc Hornstein, Chief of Police, recaps the ordinance continued from the
September 21 st Village Council meeting. A proposed amendment is presented
before Council to update the Class F liquor license allowing to accommodate
Hometown Coffee & Juice’s business model for the sale of cocktails.
   The applicant, Lou Rubin, from Hometown Coffee & Juice is present and
confirms that he has no intent of having his restaurant resemble a bar and is
comfortable with not having alcohol sales prior to 11am. Chief Hornstein
confirms Councils follow up question regarding the breakdown of the 3% of
alcohol sales and how much of that reflects cocktails. It is confirmed that the
3% of alcohol sales are split amongst cocktails, beer, and wine. The Village
Attorney has amended the Village code to allow the sale and service of alcohol
at 11am rather than the proposed 9am hour.
   Trustee Dearborn and Apatoff both agree that the 11am hours are an
improvement from 9am and do not see an issue with the amended hours.
   Loui Rubin, owner of Hometown Coffee & Juice, informs Council that alcohol
sales are not the core of their business and are looking to only add the
addition to their sales. Mr. Rubin confirms that alcohol sales reflect only a
small portion of their business sales. Trustee Apatoff questions where the
alcohol is stored within the business space that is accessible to the
customers. Mr. Rubin confirms that the alcohol is stored behind a counter, on
the Elm side of the building, where customers are able to sit and eat.
   Trustee Dalman, seconded by Trustee Mancini, moved to introduce Ordinance
No. MC-5-2021. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Apatoff,
Cripe, Dalman, Dearborn, and Mancini. Nays: None. Absent: Trustee Swierk.
   b)   Ordinance No. M-17-2021: 1225 Hill Road - Variation (Introduction/
Adoption)
   Subject property owners are requesting an approval of a zoning variation for
the approval of construction of a pergola on the property where the Zoning
Board of Appeals has voted for an approval with a 5-0 vote. Community
Development Director David Schoon confirms that the Engineering Department has
reviewed the plan and has approved it based on the stormwater detention
requirement and flood plane management requirements.
   Trustee Dalman, seconded by Trustee Mancini, moved to waive introduction of
Ordinance No. M-17-2021. By roll call vote, the motion carried Ayes: Trustees
Apatoff, Cripe, Dalman, Dearborn, and Mancini. Nays: None. Absent: Trustee
Swierk.
   Trustee Apatoff, seconded by Trustee Dearborn, moved to adopt Ordinance No.
M-17-2021. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Apatoff,
Cripe, Dalman, Dearborn, and Mancini. Nays: None. Absent: Trustee Swierk.
9)   Old Business. None.
10)   New Business. None.
11)   Appointments: None.
12)   Closed Session. None.
13)   Adjournment.
Trustee Dearborn, seconded by Trustee Apatoff, moved to adjourn the meeting. By
voice vote, the motion carried. The meeting adjourned at 7:12 PM.
 
