October 19, 2021
MINUTES
WINNETKA VILLAGE COUNCIL
REGULAR MEETING
October 19, 2021
(Approved: xx)
A record of a legally convened regular meeting of the Council of the Village of
Winnetka, which was held in the Council Chambers at Village Hall on Tuesday,
October 19, 2021, at 7:00 PM.
1)   Call to Order.
President Rintz called the meeting to order at 7:01 PM. Present: Trustees
Robert Apatoff, Andrew Cripe, Tina Dalman, Robert Dearborn, Kim Mancini, and
John Swierk. Absent: None. Also present: Village Manager Robert Bahan,
Assistant Village Manager Kristin Kazenas, Village Attorney Peter Friedman.
2)   Pledge of Allegiance.
Trustee Swierk led the group in the Pledge of Allegiance.
3   Quorum.
   a)   Friday, October 29, 2021 Budget Review Meeting. All of the Council
members present said they expect to attend.
   b)   Tuesday, November 2, 2021 Regular Meeting. All of the Council members
present said they expect to attend.
   c)   Tuesday, November 9, 2021 Study Session. All of the Council members
present said they expect to attend.
   d)   Tuesday, November 16, 2021 Regular Meeting. All of the Council members
present said they expect to attend.
4)   Public Comment. None.
5)   Reports:
   a)   Trustees. None.
   b)   Attorney. None.
   c)   Manager. Village Manager Rob Bahan informs Council that the annual
budget packets will be distributed on Thursday, October 21 st to Council
members.
   d)   Village President. President Rintz states that he attended the ribbon
cutting for Valentina and believes that the transformation from a real estate
office to the current business use is magnificent. Mr. Rintz describes the glow
of windows at night and the product display really confirms what they have been
working towards. Mr. Rintz also states that he attended the Farmers Market and
is amazed at the record number of vendors in attendance as well as the turn out
of visitors and the hallmark feel seeing the number of families and kids out.
6)   Approval of the Agenda.
Trustee Cripe, seconded by Trustee Apatoff, moved to approve the Agenda. By
voice vote, the motion carried.
7)   Consent Agenda
   a)   Village Council Minutes.
      i)   September 9, 2021, Regular Meeting.
   b)   Approval of Warrant List dated September 24, 2021 – October 7, 2021 in
the amount of $798,435.64.
   c)   Ordinance No. MC-05-2021: Amending Liquor Code (Adoption)
   d)   Resolution No. R-72-2021: Approving a Class F Liquor License for
Hometown Coffee Winnetka, LLC (Adoption)
   e)   Resolution No. R-85-2021: GIS Service Provider Agreement (Adoption)
   Trustee Dalman, seconded by Trustee Cripe, moved to approve the foregoing
items on the Consent Agenda by omnibus vote. By roll call vote, the motion
carried. Ayes: Trustees Apatoff, Cripe, Dalman, Dearborn, Mancini and Swierk.
Nays: None. Absent: None.
8)   Ordinances and Resolutions. None.
9)   Old Business. None.
10)   New Business. None.
11)   Appointments:
   a)   Appoint Heather Niehoff to a four-year term on the Design Review Board
– her term will expire 5/1/2025. Heather is filling a vacancy from Brooke
Kelly’s resignation.
   Trustee Dearborn, seconded by Trustee Cripe, moved to appoint Heather
Niehoff to the Design Review Board to fill a vacancy for Brooke Kelly. Her term
will expire on 5/1/2025. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees
Apatoff, Cripe, Dalman, Dearborn, Mancini, and Swierk. Nays: None. Absent:
None.
12)   Closed Session for the purpose of discussing (i) the disposition and
setting the price for Village property and (ii) pending litigation, pursuant to
Sections 2(c)(6) and 2(c)(11) of the Illinois Open Meetings Act.
Trustee Dalman, seconded by Trustee Dearborn moved to adjourn into Closed
Session for the purpose of discussing (i) the disposition and setting the price
for Village property and (ii) pending litigation, pursuant to Sections 2(c)(6)
and 2(c)(11) of the Illinois Open Meetings Act and to adjourn the Open Meeting
automatically and immediately upon the conclusion of the Closed Session without
the conduct of any further business or comments. Trustee Dearborn seconded the
motion. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Apatoff, Cripe,
Dalman, Dearborn, Mancini, and Swierk. Nays: None. Absent: None.
The Council adjourned into Closed Session at 7:07 PM.
13)   Adjournment.
The meeting adjourned at 8:53 PM.
 
