8)   Ordinances and Resolutions:
Resolution No. R-22-2022: Streetscape Phase 4 Contract Approval (Adoption).  
Director of Engineering Jim Bernahl is requesting Council’s approval to waive
the bidding requirements for the Construction of the Phase 4 Streetscape
project. Mr. Bernahl indicates that he would proceed with the approval of the
negotiated contract with ALamp Concrete Inc. Mr. Bernahl confirms that the
Village has budgeted $3,065,530 for the Streetscape project, briefing Council
on the total project cost of $2,926,639 which includes $2,621,449 for the A
Lamp contract, $91,000 for the transformer location, and $214,190 for long lead
time items. The total project cost of $2,926,639 compared to the budget of
$3,065,530 results in a remaining budget balance of $138,891.
Village staff will be finalizing the construction schedule and phasing with the
contractor and meeting with local businesses regarding the construction. Mr.
Bernahl confirms that the Village will host two virtual open house sessions for
the businesses ensuring that there is efficient communication.
Trustee Swierk, seconded by Trustee Cripe, moved to adopt Resolution
No. R-22-2022. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Apatoff,
Cripe, Dalman, Dearborn, Mancini, and Swierk. Nays: None. Absent: None.
Resolution No. R-23-2022: Purchase of Pedestrian Lighting (Adoption).
Director of Engineering Jim Bernahl seeks Village Councils approval to purchase
LED bollards as part of the Phase 4 Streetscape project improving the overall
lighting and enhancing the holiday lights in the West Elm business district.
This purchase includes pedestrian lights, bollards at entrance of Village Hall,
and entrance of Moffat Mall.
 
Joe Coughlin, co-founder and the editor in chief at the Record, commends
Village Council on their work.
 
Trustee Mancini, seconded by Trustee Swierk, moved to adopt Resolution
No. R-23-2022. By roll call vote, the motion carried. Ayes: Trustees Apatoff,
Cripe, Dalman, Dearborn, Mancini, and Swierk. Nays: None. Absent: None.
